 the recognition is the Silver status, and the highlight is the top seven percent global ranking. For ISS, the recognition is the Prime status. \n\nI must verify if there is any other agency. What about Sustainalytics? If I find information on Sustainalytics, I should include it, but if the data only points to the three above, I must stick to the verified ones to avoid inventing information. The current path covers the three most common and distinct types of ESG evidence. The strength of this direction lies in the triangulation of investment-grade ratings (MSCI), governance/investor-focused status (ISS), and operational/supply chain assessments (EcoVadis), providing a 360-degree view of sustainability performance. This approach covers the specific outputs required: grades, statuses, medals, and comparative percentiles.",
