ext but lacks a numerical frequency rate in the tables, it cannot be part of the answer. I must distinguish between a country being \"mentioned\" and a country being \"highlighted for its rates.\" The rate is the key identifier. I will focus my direction on identifying the specific collection of European countries that are explicitly paired with frequency rate data in the ESG safety performance tables, noting that this list comprises a specific cluster of European industrial operations including both Western and Central/Eastern European nations.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nAustria, Czech Republic, Germany, Norway, Poland, Romania, Slovakia, Switzerland<|im_end|>"
