\n\nLet's evaluate the group I am gathering. I have Claudia Sowa-Frank, Daniele Frijia, Dr. Christine Bortenlänger, Dr. Joachim Rauhut, Dr. Jürgen M. Geißinger, Gordon Riske, Heike Madan, and Josef Mailer. I need to verify if these specific people are indeed the current members of the Supervisory Board. Let me test the validity of Gordon Riske. Is he an executive or a supervisor? He is often associated with technical leadership, but if he is on the Supervisory Board, he must be listed there. Let me check Heike Madan and Josef Mailer. If Mailer is a Chairman of the Management Board, I have made a fundamental error. However, if he is the Chairman of the Supervisory Board, he belongs on the list. \n\nLet me re-verify the distinction. If I find a name like \"X\" who is the CEO, they belong to the Management Board. If \"Y\" is the Chairman of the Supervisory Board, they belong to the list. The difficulty lies in the potential overlap in public profiles where a person's name is associated with both \"MTU\" and \"Leadership,\" making it easy to conflate the two boards. I must discard any name that is explicitly linked to the \"Vorstand\" or \"Management Board.\" \n\nLet's consider a counterexample. If I included the members of the Audit Committee, would that be correct? The Audit Committee is a subgroup *of* the Supervisory Board. While their members are part of the governance structure, the question asks for the individuals contributing through their roles in the Supervisory Board, which generally refers to the full body of the board. If I only list the Audit Committee, it would be too narrow. If I list the entire board, I am covering the full scope of the governance structure requested.\n\nAnother potential error: including board members from subsidiaries. The question asks about MTU’s governance structure. This implies the parent company's board. I must filter out any directors who only represent lower-level divisions unless they serve on the main Supervisory Board. \n\nI have identified a set of names: Claudia Sowa-Frank, Daniele Frijia, Dr. Christine Bortenlänger, Dr. Joachim Rauhut, Dr. Jürgen M. Geißinger, Gordon Riske, Heike Madan, and Josef Mailer. I must check if this set represents the complete or primary membership of the Supervisory Board. I will cross-reference the names to ensure none are mistakenly pulled from the Management Board. If I look at the CEO's name and it is not on this list, I am likely on the right track. If I see that the current CEO is, for example, someone not listed here, then these individuals are indeed the oversight component. I will now perform a final check on the alignment between these names and the specific \"Supervisory Board\" designation to ensure no executive functions are being incorrectly attributed to the oversight roles.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nClaudia Sowa-Frank, Daniele Frijia, Dr. Christine Bortenlänger, Dr. Joachim Rauhut, Dr. Jürgen M. Geißinger, Gordon Riske, Heike Madan, Josef Mailer<|im_end|>"
