    "problem": "Which criteria does Frequentis AG use to evaluate supplier performance in ESG-related areas?",
    "attempt": "Frequentis AG, a leading provider of communication and information management systems for safety-critical environments, likely evaluates its suppliers based on a range of Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) criteria to ensure sustainability and ethical standards across its supply chain. While specific details may vary, companies like Frequentis typically consider the following key areas when assessing supplier performance in ESG-related areas:\n\n1. **Environmental Criteria:**\n   - Energy consumption and carbon footprint reduction strategies.\n   - Waste management practices and recycling efforts.\n   - Use of sustainable materials and resources.\n   - Compliance with environmental regulations and certifications.\n\n2. **Social Criteria:**\n   - Labor rights and working conditions, including fair wages and safe work environments.\n   - Diversity and inclusion initiatives within the workforce.\n   - Community engagement and support programs.\n   - Health and safety measures for employees and the community.\n\n3. **Governance Criteria:**\n   - Corporate governance structure and transparency.\n   - Ethical business practices, including anti-corruption policies.\n   - Supply chain management and traceability.\n   - Risk management and compliance with legal requirements.\n\nFrequentis would likely integrate these criteria into their supplier evaluation process through questionnaires, audits, and regular assessments. The company might also require suppliers to adhere to specific guidelines or standards that align with international best practices and frameworks such as the United Nations Global Compact, ISO 26000, or other relevant industry-specific standards.\n\nFor precise and up-to-date information regarding Frequentis AG's specific supplier evaluation criteria, it would be advisable to refer directly to their official corporate responsibility reports or contact their procurement department.",
    "solution": "Price: e.g. development of prices and comparison with the previous year and market prices, Quality: e.g. product quality, product complexity, quality assurance system, Support quality: e.g. commercial, personal, and technical support, Sustainability of the supplier, business environment (stability, performance, flexibility, environmental management, etc.), environment-friendly and sustainable packaging, social aspects (CSR code, social competence, etc.)",
