    "problem": "Which countries are part of the ESG reporting scope for UNIQA's operations?",
    "attempt": "UNIQA, an Austrian insurance company, typically follows global best practices and regulatory requirements when it comes to Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) reporting. However, the specific countries included in its ESG reporting scope can vary based on where it operates and has significant business activities.\n\nAs of my last update, UNIQA operates primarily in Central and Eastern Europe, including Austria, Germany, the Czech Republic, Slovakia, Hungary, Slovenia, Croatia, Serbia, Romania, Bulgaria, and Turkey. Therefore, these countries would likely be part of its ESG reporting scope. It's important to note that UNIQA may also consider other factors such as supply chain locations and investment portfolios when determining the full extent of its ESG reporting.\n\nFor the most accurate and up-to-date information, you should refer directly to UNIQA's latest sustainability reports or contact their corporate communications department.",
    "solution": "Albania, Austria, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Croatia, Czechia, Hungary, Kosovo, Liechtenstein, Montenegro, North Macedonia, Poland, Romania, Russia, Serbia, Slovakia, Switzerland, Ukraine",
