y's formal grievance procedure. I need to ensure I am not creating a list of synonyms. A compliance officer and an HR manager have different objectives: one focuses on legal/ethical risk, the other on personnel/operational management. A works council focuses on employee rights. These are distinct actors with different motivations.\n\nOne more check: does \"reporting systems\" cover both the digital tool and the manual processes? Yes. I should avoid saying \"the employee reports to the system\" and instead say \"the employee uses reporting systems such as...\" to show the relationship between the mechanism and the actor. The strongest direction involves categorizing these by the type of protection they offer: direct hierarchy, professional administration, independent oversight, and labor representation, all facilitated by specific mechanisms like digital tools.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nHR department, compliance officer, digital whistleblower system, line manager, ombudsman, reporting systems, works council<|im_end|>"
