    "problem": "Which family-related policies and programmes demonstrate Addiko's commitment to employee well-being?",
    "attempt": "It seems there might be some confusion in your query as \"Addiko\" is not widely recognized as a company known for specific family-related policies or programs that are commonly discussed. If you're referring to a specific organization named Addiko Bank or another entity under the Addiko Group, which operates in Central and Eastern Europe, they do indeed have a focus on corporate social responsibility and employee welfare.\n\nHowever, without specific details about the exact policies or programs you're asking about, I can provide a general overview of what companies often implement to support their employees' family well-being:\n\n1. **Flexible Working Hours**: Allowing employees to adjust their work schedules to better accommodate family needs.\n2. **Remote Work Options**: Providing the ability to work from home or other remote locations to reduce commuting time and stress.\n3. **Parental Leave**: Offering generous parental leave policies to help new parents adjust to their roles.\n4. **Childcare Support**: Providing on-site childcare services or subsidies for external childcare.\n5. **Employee Assistance Programs (EAPs)**: Offering counseling and support services to help employees manage personal and professional challenges.\n6. **Health and Wellness Programs**: Implementing initiatives aimed at improving physical and mental health, which can include family wellness components.\n7. **Family-Friendly Facilities**: Creating spaces within the workplace that cater to families, such as nursing rooms or play areas for children.\n\nIf you could provide more context or clarify which specific company or organization you're referring to, I would be able to give a more accurate and detailed response regarding their specific family-related policies and programs.",
