ed, faith, political conviction, nationality, language, socioeconomic/family status, and military service, while distinguishing them from the organizational culture that manages them. Measurement of these factors requires a balance between identity protection and the need for data to track equity.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nculture, disability status, ethnicity, faiths, gender identity, language, military service, mindset, nationality, political conviction, race, religion or creed, sexual orientation, socioeconomic and family status<|im_end|>"
