 codes like 3.5, 4.20, and 6.5, and specific operational categories like new construction and vehicle fleets. To ensure the strongest solution, I must not group these into broad sectors like energy or transport, as that would lose the granularity required by the term economic activity. The most robust way to approach this is to capture the exact items mentioned as being subject to the assessment, maintaining the distinction between the descriptive labels and the numeric identifiers. I will focus on synthesizing these specific, non-overlapping elements into a complete list.",
