assification? One might argue that activities not mentioned in the taxonomy are a classification. However, those activities are essentially outside the framework's jurisdiction. The question asks for the classifications of economic activities under the framework, which implies looking at the statuses defined by the regulatory logic itself. The core functional distinction used by actors to report and analyze data is the gap between being able to be considered under the rules and actually meeting the requirements of the rules. This distinction separates the scope of the taxonomy from the actual sustainability performance of the activity. The first term describes the reach of the regulation, while the second term describes the degree of compliance with its specific environmental standards. This dual-layered classification is the only way to provide the granular data that the taxonomy is designed to produce for the financial markets.",
