's role is to provide the necessary transparency for stakeholders to assess the governance quality of the financial data underpinning the environmental disclosures. I have identified that the connection is not about the environmental criteria themselves, but about the governance-led validation of the financial inputs. The reconciliation uses the relationship between profit, the reporting period, and the weighted rates to provide this validation. I will now focus on how these specific mathematical components serve as the evidence for governance reliability.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nactual tax expenses, profit before income taxes, reporting period, weighted domestic and foreign tax rate<|im_end|>"
