hat specifically refine the thresholds set in the initial climate-related act. I must look for the recent updates to the climate-related delegated act. I recall there were significant updates in 2023. I need to identify the specific regulation numbers for these amendments. I am looking for two delegated regulations from 2023 that revise the climate-related technical screening criteria. These would be Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2485 and Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2486. I need to verify if these two acts specifically target the technical screening criteria within the 2021/2139 framework. If they do, they satisfy the requirement for amendments. The mechanism is clear: the Commission uses these delegated acts to refine the technical thresholds as data or political consensus evolves. By combining the original delegated regulation that set the criteria with the two subsequent regulations that amended them, I cover both components of the question. I must be careful not to include the implementing regulations that deal with disclosure and reporting, as those are different in mechanism and output, focusing on how information is presented rather than the technical thresholds themselves. The strongest path is to link the base climate-related delegated regulation with its two specific amending counterparts.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nDelegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2139, Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2485, Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2486<|im_end|>"
