ular implementation. \n\nI should check if I am confusing this with the Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation. The SFDR is a major part of the ESG regulatory landscape, but its role is to regulate how financial market participants disclose information. While it relies on the Taxonomy, it is not the source of the definition for enabling activities. Similarly, the CSRD is about the obligation to report, not the definition of the activity's sustainability status. Therefore, the focus must remain strictly within the Taxonomy's own hierarchy of laws.\n\nI must ensure that I am not just picking these because they sound like standard legal citations. I need to verify the causal link. The Taxonomy Regulation establishes the rule, Article 10(1)(i) defines the specific condition for enabling, and the Implementing Regulation (EU IR 2023/2485) provides the technical enforcement. This triad covers the objective, the mechanism, and the procedure. The strongest solution direction involves identifying this specific intersection between the parent regulation, the detailed article-level provision, and the recent implementing regulation that operationalizes the enabling activity criteria.",
