company conducted a formal review of its activities against the technical screening criteria to satisfy the Do No Significant Harm principle. This process ensures that the benefits gained in one area, like climate change mitigation through energy-efficient hosting, are not offset by significant harm to other objectives, such as water protection or the circular economy. This analysis is the essential regulatory bridge that allows a company to claim taxonomy alignment, as the framework requires proof of both substantial contribution and the absence of significant harm across all applicable environmental objectives.",
