    "problem": "What was the monetary value and percentage of OpEx for 'Installation, maintenance and repair of instruments and devices for measuring, regulation and controlling energy performance of buildings' (CCM-7.5) under Taxonomy-eligible but not aligned (A.2) activities?",
    "attempt": "To provide an accurate answer to your question regarding the monetary value and percentage of OpEx (Operating Expenditure) for 'Installation, maintenance and repair of instruments and devices for measuring, regulation and controlling energy performance of buildings' (CCM-7.5) under Taxonomy-eligible but not aligned (A.2) activities, I would need specific data from financial reports or detailed analyses that categorize expenditures according to the EU Taxonomy criteria.\n\nThe EU Taxonomy Regulation provides a classification system for economic activities that make substantial contributions to climate change mitigation and adaptation. However, certain activities can be considered Taxonomy-eligible but not aligned if they do not fully meet the technical screening criteria set out in the regulation. CCM-7.5 falls into this category if it does not comply with the specific criteria related to energy efficiency improvements in buildings.\n\nWithout access to specific financial data, it's impossible to give exact figures. Typically, such information would be found in detailed sustainability reports or financial disclosures where companies break down their expenses according to environmental impact categories as defined by the EU Taxonomy.\n\nIf you have access to a company's sustainability report or financial statements that include this level of detail, you could find the specific figures there. Alternatively, consulting with a financial analyst who specializes in sustainability reporting could provide the necessary insights based on available data.",
    "solution": "'Installation, maintenance and repair of instruments and devices for measuring, regulation and controlling energy performance of buildings' (CCM-7.5) under Taxonomy-eligible but not aligned (A.2) activities accounted for TEUR 1,255, representing 4% of total OpEx.",
