    "attempt": "The WELL Health-Safety Rating is designed to help organizations implement and document actions that can be taken to support the health and well-being of their occupants during the ongoing coronavirus pandemic and beyond. While it focuses on health and safety measures, it also aligns with broader principles of sustainability and human health outcomes. The rating evaluates several key areas:\n\n1. **Cleaning and Sanitization Strategies**: This includes the implementation of effective cleaning protocols, use of appropriate products, and frequency of cleaning in high-touch areas.\n\n2. **Emergency Preparedness Programs**: Organizations must have plans in place for responding to emergencies, including pandemics, natural disasters, and other crises that could impact the health and safety of occupants.\n\n3. **Health Service Resources**: Providing access to health services and resources, such as telemedicine options, mental health support, and educational materials about health and wellness.\n\n4. **Air and Water Quality Management**: Ensuring that air and water quality meet or exceed relevant standards and guidelines to protect occupant health.\n\n5. **Stakeholder Engagement and Communication**: Effective communication strategies to keep stakeholders informed about health and safety measures, policies, and any changes that may affect them.\n\n6. **Operational Integration**: Integrating health and safety practices into daily operations, ensuring they become part of the organizational culture and routine.\n\n7. **Design Interventions**: Implementing design features that enhance health and safety, such as improved ventilation systems, touchless technology, and flexible spaces that can accommodate social distancing.\n\n8. **Physical and Mental Health**: Promoting physical and mental health through various initiatives, such as ergonomic workstations, fitness programs, and stress management workshops.\n\nWhile these criteria focus primarily on immediate health and safety concerns, they also contribute to long-term sustainability by promoting healthier environments and behaviors. For instance, improving air and water quality not only protects against infectious diseases but also supports overall environmental health. Similarly, encouraging physical activity and mental well-being can lead to more productive and resilient communities over time.",
