ographical approach, whereas the Polish metrics are referred to more generally as figures for Poland. This suggests that the German evaluation has a higher level of granularity. I initially thought the scope was limited to where the company owns buildings, but the presence of business operations and administrative sites means the scope must include both the real estate assets and the corporate infrastructure. I reject the idea that the answer is only the countries because it misses the specific asset and administrative divisions. I also reject the idea that it is only the properties because it misses the corporate operations. The most effective path is to define the scope as a combination of asset-based regions, specifically the German and Polish portfolios, the operational presence in Germany, the administrative sites, and the overarching organizational scope of the group. This approach accounts for the different levels of aggregation and the distinction between property-based and operation-based metrics.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nGerman portfolio, Polish rental portfolio, ROBYG Vantage Group, business operations in Germany, figures for Poland, overall portfolio in Germany, own administrative locations<|im_end|>"
