ted elements used to frame the environmental impact and the social dimension of water management. A more robust approach involves categorizing the text into different functional layers. I need to distinguish between the objective, such as achieving Sustainable Solutions for Tomorrow, the mechanism, such as Smart Rainwater Management, and the underlying environmental driver, such as water scarcity. I also need to recognize when the text uses a heading to bridge two different domains, like the intersection of Energy and Water. The difficulty lies in deciding whether to group these or keep them as distinct highlighted topics. If the text presents them as a single unit, they must be treated as a single topic. I must also check if terms like Sustainable water management are being used as a general descriptor or as a specific highlighted theme. The strongest direction for a solution is to perform a semantic scan that identifies these various layers—policy, technology, resource nexus, and environmental condition—while treating the specific phrasing used in the text as the definitive identifier of the topic. This requires looking for both the technical procedures and the high-level strategic frameworks.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nEnergy and Water, Every Drop Counts, National Water Reuse Action Plan, Smart Rainwater Management, Sustainable Solutions for Tomorrow, Sustainable water management, water scarcity<|im_end|>"
