 represents the industry's voice, and one provides specialized ecological knowledge. A robust solution must capture this variety. The strongest direction is to categorize the search by these functional roles: certification/standard-setting bodies, regulatory/advisory bodies, industry-specific committees, and specialized ecological or waste management associations. This multi-pronged approach ensures that the exchange of expertise is captured across the entire spectrum of sustainability, from high-level policy to ground-level material science. I will focus the final verification on confirming that PORR's specific engagement with these types of entities is documented through membership or active participation.",
