ould fit this profile. This is a different mechanism of collaboration—technical and specialized rather than political or standard-setting.\n\nI should evaluate if these categories are truly distinct. They are. One sets the standards, one sets the rules, one represents the industry's voice, and one provides specialized ecological knowledge. A robust solution must capture this variety. The strongest direction is to categorize the search by these functional roles: certification/standard-setting bodies, regulatory/advisory bodies, industry-specific committees, and specialized ecological or waste management associations. This multi-pronged approach ensures that the exchange of expertise is captured across the entire spectrum of sustainability, from high-level policy to ground-level material science. I will focus the final verification on confirming that PORR's specific engagement with these types of entities is documented through membership or active participation.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nBienenlieb, Deutsche Gesellschaft für nachhaltiges Bauen (DGNB), Gesellschaft für Ökologie und Abfallwirtschaft, Umweltausschuss der Deutschen Bauindustrie, Umweltbundesamt, Umweltdachverhand, Umweltschutzverband, Österreichische Gesellschaft für Nachhaltige Immobilienwirtschaft (ÖGNI)<|im_end|>"
