he specific mechanisms mentioned. The UAE's large-scale solar integration into its energy grid can be viewed as a way to meet sustainability goals through both utility-scale procurement and potentially onsite industrial applications.\n\nI will reject the idea that this is a list of all renewable-rich countries. That would include China and Norway, which are not in my target set. The specificity of the mechanisms—tariffs and onsite generation—must be the filter. The strongest direction is to look for regions where there is a documented intersection of regulatory support for renewable pricing and a high rate of decentralized or industrial renewable energy adoption, as reported in specific sustainability or ESG performance datasets.",
