    "problem": "Which certifications reflect the sustainability standards of the office buildings mentioned in the context?",
    "attempt": "To accurately answer your question, I would need more specific information about the context you're referring to, including details about the office buildings and any particular certifications that were mentioned or are relevant. However, some common certifications that reflect sustainability standards for office buildings include:\n\n1. **LEED (Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design)**: This is one of the most widely recognized green building certification programs. It provides third-party verification that a building was designed and built using strategies aimed at improving performance across various metrics such as energy savings, water efficiency, CO2 emissions reduction, improved indoor environmental quality, and stewardship of resources and sensitivity to their impacts.\n\n2. **BREEAM (Building Research Establishment Environmental Assessment Method)**: BREEAM is the leading sustainability assessment method for master planning projects, infrastructure, and buildings. It sets the standard for best practice in sustainable design, construction, and operation and has been used for nearly 30 years across the world.\n\n3. **WELL Building Standard**: This focuses on enhancing people's health and well-being through better building design, operations, and management. It covers areas like air, water, nourishment, light, fitness, comfort, and mind.\n\n4. **Green Star**: Developed by the Green Building Council of Australia, this rating system assesses the environmental design and impact of buildings, fitouts, and communities. It is used in Australia and New Zealand.\n\n5. **ENERGY STAR**: While primarily focused on energy efficiency, ENERGY STAR can also be applied to commercial buildings and industrial plants to measure overall energy performance.\n\nIf you could provide more specific details about the office buildings and the context you're referring to, I could give a more precise answer regarding which certifications apply.",
    "solution": "German Sustainable Building Council (DGNB), Gold certificate, International WELL Building Institute, Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED), Platinum standard, WELL Gold Core & Shell certificate",
