he vehicle at different stages of its lifecycle. The first layer is the selection of the asset through procurement, the second is the maintenance of the asset's physical properties through specific consumables, and the third is the optimization of the asset's operation through behavioral management. I will focus on developing a solution that explores how these three distinct domains—procurement, technical maintenance of consumables, and behavioral training—work together to reduce the mechanical and human-induced inefficiencies in fuel usage.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nCourse on fuel efficiency, Eco-tuning, Procured fuel-efficient vehicles, assessing consumption of individual vehicles, engine oil, fuel-saving tires<|im_end|>"
