duct innovation, digital intelligence, and strategic business management. I must ensure that the software competence centre, specifically linked to Tridonic, is viewed as a distinct and essential domain because it represents a different technological layer than traditional lighting R&D. The connection between software and sustainability is the intelligence required for energy-efficient, automated lighting ecosystems.\n\nI have tested the technical-only path and rejected it for being too narrow. I have tested the digital-only path and rejected it for being too specialized. I have tested the governance-only path and rejected it for being too detached from the product. The most robust direction is a multi-disciplinary approach that captures the physical, digital, and strategic pillars of the group's future. The domains must include the creation of the product, the digital control of the product, the management of the product's market presence, and the financial governance of the group's resources. This encompasses the full spectrum of a modern ESG-driven corporate strategy.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nBrand & portfolio management for the lighting brands, Corporate IT, Corporate finance, Research & development for the lighting brands, Research & development for the software competence centre (Tridonic)<|im_end|>"
