ifferently, perhaps through different product lines or local subsidiaries. But I must not invent facts. I need to look for the intersection of Wienerberger's regional sustainability reports and Habitat's regional partner recognitions. The strongest direction is to cross-reference the specific countries mentioned in Wienerberger's annual ESG or sustainability disclosures with the chapters of Habitat for Humanity that have officially recognized them as a partner. This will filter out the countries where they merely sell products and isolate the ones where the specific collaboration is actually occurring. This approach respects the distinction between a customer relationship and a CSR partnership.",
