TF for automotive, ISO 17025 for testing, and the various branches of NADCAP for aerospace processes, does it form a cohesive set? The common thread is that these are all high-barrier-to-entry certifications required by major OEMs to ensure that their supply chains are reliable, which is a core component of governance and operational sustainability. A generic approach would fail because it wouldn't provide the technical assurance required by the actors in these specific industries. The strongest direction for a solution lies in identifying the intersection of sector-specific quality management systems and the technical accreditation of special processes and testing methodologies used in high-consequence manufacturing supply chains.",
