r is a foundation, whereas net zero is a destination. If I list the ESG spectrum as a commitment, I fail because the spectrum is a range of topics, not a promise of action.\n\nThe most robust way to structure the solution is to identify the overarching strategy name to provide context, then separate the structural pillars—which include both the thematic scope of the ESG spectrum and the core operational mechanism of transforming banking operations—from the specific commitments, which include the climate-related targets and the nature of their voluntary undertakings. This approach ensures that the distinction between the \"what\" (the ESG scope), the \"how\" (the banking transformation), and the \"to what end\" (net zero and climate combat) is maintained. This direction allows for a comprehensive answer that avoids the trap of treating the entire strategy as a single list of items.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nStrategy 2027, ambitious net zero targets, commitment to combating climate change, sustainability spectrum of environmental, social and governance, sustainable transformation of our banking operations, voluntary undertakings<|im_end|>"
