e alive. The most robust solution direction therefore involves a combination of structural knowledge-sharing mechanisms, such as specialized committees, and a targeted talent pipeline of young physicists, designed specifically to ensure that the technical depth of radiation physics is transferred and preserved despite the shrinking operational landscape of the nuclear energy sector.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nactive committees, knowledge about radiation protection topics, phasing out of nuclear energy, preservation of professional competence, radiation physics, young skilled physicists<|im_end|>"
