re the employees (the laborers and learners) and the local organizations (the experts and facilitators). The procedures are the presentation and the beach cleaning. The outputs are the physical refuse and the cognitive shift in awareness. Is there a counterexample? What if the education happened on a different day? If the education and the cleanup were decoupled, the impact on awareness would likely be diluted. The synergy depends on the proximity of the intellectual input to the physical output. The partnership is critical because it provides the necessary local expertise to facilitate this specific, synchronized experience. The strength of this direction lies in the causal link: the partnership provides the expertise, the expertise provides the education, and the education, when paired with the physical labor, creates the heightened awareness. This addresses both parts of the prompt through a single, unified mechanism.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nEmployees in Peru and Ecuador partnered with local environmental organizations, attended a presentation on ocean ecological challenges, and cleaned a local beach, collecting 433 kilograms of refuse. Their efforts highlighted both education and impactful action.<|im_end|>"
