aterial processes of the metal and coal lighter factories to the physical mechanism of leaching, and then using this to illustrate how the historical failure to internalize environmental costs demonstrates the economic and social necessity of modern sustainable industrial management. This path addresses the cause, the specific substances involved, and the systemic lesson required.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nThe site housed a machine and metal goods factory and a coal lighter factory with melting pots for naphthalene between 1898 and 1982. These activities caused contamination of the soil and groundwater due to industrial processes and materials used.<|im_end|>"
