l matters are direct outputs, while the legal matter is a conditional trigger. This leads to the conclusion that the factual matters are the ones that are universally required, or cap-covered, for both size groups.\n**Final Answer**\n<|im_start|>answer\nIt discloses that employees receive pay equal to or above the applicable minimum wage, reports 0% coverage by collective bargaining agreements, and reports the average annual training hours per employee. It need not disclose the female-to-male pay gap because that datapoint applies only when EU law or other national regulation already requires the undertaking to report it. Annex II covers the minimum-pay answer, collective-bargaining coverage and average training hours for both size groups; it does not list the conditional pay-gap datapoint.<|im_end|>"
